Chapter: SmpPreempt

 Six children spin without ever yielding: no channel, no wait, no exit
 until the work is done. On a core that cannot be preempted, such a child
 runs to completion uninterrupted. Every timer interrupt taken on a core
 whose id is not zero adds one to cell 36216 with a locked add.

Section: Body

  spin : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin (n) (acc) = if n == 0 then acc else spin (n - 1) (acc + 1)

  child-body : Integer -> Integer
  child-body (x) = spin 1000000000 0

  opening : [Console, Concurrent] Nothing = act
    a <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    b <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    c <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    d <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    e <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    f <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    wa <- process-wait a
    wb <- process-wait b
    wc <- process-wait c
    wd <- process-wait d
    we <- process-wait e
    wf <- process-wait f
    print-line-uni (if atomic-load 36200 > 0
                    then "an ap ran a process"
                    else "NO AP RAN A PROCESS")
    print-line-uni (if atomic-load 36216 > 0
                    then "an ap was preempted"
                    else "NO AP WAS PREEMPTED")
  end
